|> Exercise
    handle=_dimensional_f_g_f_

    What constraints does the composition
    $$
    f \circ g \circ f
    $$
    impose on the signatures of $f$ and $g$?

    |> Solution

        The composition requires $f$ and $g$ of the
        form

        $$
        \begin{gathered}
        f : [\tA] \ra [\tB] \\
        \up{1.6}g : [\tB] \ra [\tA]
        \end{gathered}
        $$

        for some units A and B, as the output of $f$
        is passed to $g$ and the output of $g$ is passed to $f$.

        !! Formally, parsing 
        
        !! $$
        !! f \circ g \circ f
        !! $$

        !! as

        !! $$
        !! f \circ (g \circ f)
        !! $$

        !! the subexpression “$g \circ f$” implies
        !! units of the form 

        !! $$
        !! \begin{gathered}
        !! f : [\A] \ra [\B] \\
        !! \up{1.6}g : [\B] \ra [\C]
        !! \end{gathered}
        !! $$

        !! but then $(g \circ f)$ has output units C,
        !! and the further composition with $f$ implies
        !! $\C = \A$. (The alternate parsing

        !! $$
        !! (f \circ g) 
        !! $$
